hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-12 = cons "*Screen* comes through Middle Dutch from a word meaning shield, protection: a screen was first something you put between yourself and heat or wind. Today's screen also shields, mostly the device's operator from the person, the dark direction. A screen that is an interface turns the shield into a face: what's between you and the system becomes the place where you meet it." (cons "" nil)
